# 7. COMPLETE USER WORKFLOW

The most important part of DataKriti is the complete end-to-end experience.

Implement this workflow:

STEP 1: User opens DataKriti.

STEP 2: User uploads a Kannada document.

STEP 3: Application validates the file and previews it.

STEP 4: Recovery Intelligence evaluates document quality.

STEP 5: Application recommends or performs enhancement.

STEP 6: User compares original and enhanced images.

STEP 7: User initiates Kannada OCR.

STEP 8: Extracted Kannada text appears in the verification editor.

STEP 9: Confidence indicators identify text that needs review.

STEP 10: User corrects uncertain text.

STEP 11: Corrected text becomes the source for subsequent AI operations.

STEP 12: User translates the document into any of the eight target languages.

STEP 13: User generates a summary.

STEP 14: User extracts important information.

STEP 15: User asks questions about the document.

STEP 16: AI answers with source references.

STEP 17: User listens to the Kannada text.

STEP 18: User exports the processed document.

STEP 19: The document is saved in the searchable library.

STEP 20: The saved document and extracted text remain available offline where supported.

This workflow must work without requiring the user to upload the same document repeatedly.

